/-! Scaled diagram integrals for the proof of the contact identity (paper B §2.2, l.149-175; paper A Lemma 3.4).
The proof changes the unit of length pair by pair: the factor of the pair `a < b` is taken at scale `s a b`
(`1[|x_a-x_b| < s a b]` for an edge of `H`, `1[|x_a-x_b| ≥ s a b]` for a pair of `F`). With all scales `1` these
are `contactWeight`, `VHF`, `contactWeightExcept`, `Vpin` of `Def_HardDiskB5_Lean_Vpin`; B's `V(ε)` is `VHFsc H F (fun _ _ => 1 + ε)`,
B's `V_l(ε)` is `VHFsc` with the scales `1 + ε` on the first `l` pairs and `1` on the others, and B's `f_l(y; ε)` is
`VpinSc H F s i j y` (the pinned integral without the factor of `ij`, `x_i = 0`, `x_j = y`).
Integrands are products of indicators of open/closed sets (bounded, measurable); for connected `H` the support is
bounded, as for `VHF`/`Vpin`. -/

